{
 "what": "Reference occupied-orbital energies, heats of formation and ionisation potentials for the 42 decks in verification/decks, used by scripts/verify.mjs.",
 "provenance": {
  "producedBy": "energy-eval/mopac/scripts/mopac7.mjs --wasm (September 2026)",
  "mopacVersion": "7.01",
  "mopacSource": "the Ghemical packaging of MOPAC 7.01 (mopac7-1.15.tar.gz, Fedora lookaside md5 7e509fd03154b37cc682593365c233f4), translated with the same f2c and compiled with the same emscripten",
  "caveat": "This repository builds MOPAC 7.00 from openmopac/MOPAC-archive, a DIFFERENT release of MOPAC 7 from the one that produced these numbers. Differences of order 1e-3 eV are expected and are the 7.00-vs-7.01 delta, not a wasm defect. The bit-level wasm check is the wasm-against-native A/B in scripts/verify.mjs, which runs the identical f2c output on both targets.",
  "printingResolution": "MOPAC 7 prints eigenvalues to 3 decimals, so 0.0005 eV is the floor of any comparison and ~0.0017 eV is the resolution of a rounded difference.",
  "geometries": "cheminfo lcao photoelectron reference set, 14 molecules; the decks carry the geometry verbatim.",
  "keywords": "<METHOD> 1SCF XYZ VECTORS ALLVEC DEBUG PRECISE GEO-OK CHARGE=0 -- ALLVEC needs DEBUG because wrtkey.f calls ALLVEC unknown while matou1.f honours it; without both, MOPAC prints only a window of roots around the HOMO."
 },
